s through the point where $(x,y,z)=(-1,0,1)$ can be found by computing \n$∇f(-1,0,1).$ \n\nSo, we first find the gradient and evaluate it at $(x,y,z)=(-1,0,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\text{ }j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})\\,j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})\\,k \\\\  & =2x\\text{ }i+2y\\text{ }j+2z\\text{ }k \\\\ ∇f(-1,0,1) & =2(-1)\\,i+2(0)\\,j+2(1)\\,k \\\\  & =-2\\,i+2\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $-2\\,i+2\\,k$ is perpendicular to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=(-1,0,1).$" 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186398954 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398955 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186398954 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398956 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186398954 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398957 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186398954 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398958 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186398954 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398959 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186398954 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186398954 1077 "selection" 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186398954 1079 #edb/ref 17592186398959 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186398954 1080 #uuid "e4b666e0-c6c9-5c9c-b88e-9912d89e0283" 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186398955 1081 "-2\\,i+j+2\\,k" 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186398955 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186398955 1084 #uuid "dc0eea45-e863-58d6-862a-727382209bd0" 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186398956 1081 "-2\\,i-j+2\\,k" 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186398956 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186398956 1084 #uuid "f143a8ac-50ee-51ef-b268-61d02a927238" 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186398957 1081 "2\\,i+2\\,k" 13194139533476