 & 0 & -7 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186398986 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186398986 1084 #uuid "4b82a1dd-a8a6-5b78-82c9-fa1f39c4845b" 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186398987 1081 "B=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 3\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186398987 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186398987 1084 #uuid "7585a86b-d9f0-55bc-8e6f-efb92e7d43c2" 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186398988 1068 #edb/ref 17592186398989 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186398988 1069 "q-74650" 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186398988 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186398988 1071 "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is consistent dependent:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 2x+6y=4 \\\\  & x+(k+1)y=2\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186398988 1072 #uuid "2b1df7fe-03a7-50e4-93e7-ab9ba910308e" 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186398988 1074 "The augmented matrix for this system is \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 & 4 \\\\ 1 & k+1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 & 4 \\\\ 1 & k+1 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-\\frac{1}{2}){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 & 4 \\\\ 0 & k-2 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 2x+6y=4 \\\\  & (k-2)y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is consistent dependent if it has infinitely many solutions. For the system to have infinitely many solutions, it must have at least one free variable.\n\nIf $k=2,$ then the second equation is $0=0,$ which is true for any value of $y.$ So, we can remove this equation from the system. As a result, the system will contain only one equation, $2x+6y=4.$  \n\nThen, the basic variable will be $x,$ and we will have a free variable $y.$ That means the system will have infinitely many solutions.\n\nTherefore, our system is consistent dependent when $k=2.$" 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186398989 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398990 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186398989 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398991 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186398989 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398992 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186398989 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398993 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186398989 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398994 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186398989 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186398989 1077 "selection" 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186398989 1079 #edb/ref 17592186398993 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186398989 1080 #uuid "ce520123-e722-5fc8-b4b5-0ce963a1fe4b" 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186398990 1081 "k=\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186398990 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186398990 1084 #uuid "e3df6cd2-68c7-5027-b94c-cebc3edbefd0" 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186398991 1081 "k=-\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186398991 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186398991 1084 #uuid "3d7403d1-9523-59ef-892c-8762070fc770" 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186398992 1081 "k=-2" 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186398992 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186398992 1084 #uuid "43b3ca27-4022-5e94-91a9-05d77b4b0c3b" 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186398993 1081 "k=2" 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186398993 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186398993 1084 #uuid "321a43c8-209e