uuid "bfd92570-bd08-5565-9c64-935de2ba2369" 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186399056 1074 "To determine the intervals of continuity of a function, we take the domain of the function and exclude any points of discontinuity.\n\nThe function is defined on the intervals $(-\\infty ,3),$  and $(3,\\infty ).$ There is a discontinuity at $x=3$  but this is already excluded.  \n\nThere is also a discontinuity at $x=-3,$ so we need to exclude that.\n\nTherefore, the function is continuous on the intervals $(-\\infty ,-3),$ $(-3,3),$  and $(3,\\infty ).$ It is also continuous on any subinterval of these intervals. \n\nAmong the answer choices, the correct one is the following:\n\n$\\,$ $(-2,3)$ \n\nNotice that:\n\n- $(-3,4)$ and $(0,5)$ contain the excluded point $x=3,$ so the function is not continuous on these intervals.\n\n- $(-\\infty ,-2)$ and  $(-\\infty ,0)$ contain the point of discontinuity $x=-3$, so the function is not continuous on these intervals." 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186399057 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399058 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186399057 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399059 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186399057 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399060 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186399057 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399061 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186399057 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399062 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186399057 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186399057 1077 "selection" 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186399057 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399060 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186399057 1080 #uuid "ad20513b-7f6b-51c1-b3e8-54f31e6cfac0" 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186399058 1081 "(-\\infty ,-2)" 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186399058 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186399058 1084 #uuid "7db323bd-027d-5a72-8744-915dc9466d84" 13194139533476 1759218604558