 equations with the augmented matrix $M$ which we reduce to its row echelon form using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & -8 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -8 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & -8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we obtain ${x}_{1}=2{x}_{2}.$ Hence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, setting ${x}_{2}=1,$ we get the eigenvector \n\n$$\n{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, $P=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186399131 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399132 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186399131 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399133 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186399131 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399134 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186399131 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399135 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186399131 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399136 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186399131 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186399131 1077 "selection" 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186399131 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399133 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186399131 1080 #uuid "a57196c6-f2e4-585a-92ce-6d08ae5e8dd1" 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186399132 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186399132 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186399132 1084 #uuid "4b30d639-ee9f-5dd6-a783-78b787a8dd54" 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186399133 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186399133 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139