uations given by\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]x(t).\n$$\n\nGiven that the solution to the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ a\\end{aligned}]{e}^{5t}+{c}_{2}([\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ a\\end{aligned}]t{e}^{5t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ b\\end{aligned}]{e}^{5t}),\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R,\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $a+b?$" 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186399144 1072 #uuid "8179a1bc-9dd2-5c9c-a7dd-3de3a7cd250c" 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186399144 1074 "We need to find the eigenvalues and the eigenvectors of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSince $A$ is upper-triangular, the repeated eigenvalue is $\\lambda =5$ (of multiplicity two).\nFor this eigenvalue, we get \n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n$v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSince we have a repeated eigenvalue $\\lambda $ and only one linearly independent eigenvector $v$, the solution of the system of differential equations is given by\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}v{e}^{\\lambda t}+{c}_{2}(vt{e}^{\\lambda t}+w{e}^{\\lambda t}\\,),\n$$\n\nwhere $w$ is a solution to the equation $(A-\\lambda I)w=v.$\n\nTo find $w,$ we solve the equation $(A-\\lambda I)w=v$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A-\\lambda I)w & =v \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}5-5 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5-5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{w}_{1} \\\\ {w}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{w}_{1} \\\\ {w}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe last equality allows us to form the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}0{w}_{1}+2{w}_{2}=1 \\\\ 0{w}_{1}+0{w}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n{w}_{2}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nThe variable ${w}_{1}$ is a free variable. Setting ${w}_{1}=0,$ we get \n\n$$\nw=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is given by\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{5t}+{c}_{2}([\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]t{e}^{5t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]{e}^{5t}),\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nFinally, we see that $a=0,b=\\frac{1}{2},$ and $a+b=\\frac{1}{2}.$" 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186399145 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399146 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186399145 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399147 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186399145 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399148 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186399145 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399149 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186399145 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399150 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186399145 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186399145 1077 "selection" 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186399145 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399146 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186399145 1080 #uuid "d2967834-56c7-54af-a045-1eb688f37565" 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186399146 1081 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186399146 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186399146 1084 #uuid "66613f28-b688-5af5-87c4-a12f46f9bd0f" 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186399147 1081 "-\\frac{3}{2}" 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186399147 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186399147 1084 #uuid "b467a51e-f9be-5bed-89bc-7ff012c894de" 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186399148 1081 "2" 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186399148 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186399148 1084 #uuid "149698b5-3361-5f52-a32c-6ed656acfe8f" 13194139533476 17592186045585 true] [17592186399149 1081 "0" 13